.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt DTFL_TRACE_STATS_GET 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_trace_stats_get
.Nd report the shape of a trace
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/arrange.h
.Bd -literal
typedef struct dtfl_trace_stats {
	size_t size;
	size_t layers;
	size_t batches;
	size_t pending;
	size_t merges;
	size_t updates;
	size_t bytes;
} dtfl_trace_stats;
.Ed
.Ft int
.Fn dtfl_trace_stats_get "const dtfl_trace *t" "dtfl_trace_stats *out"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dtfl_trace_stats_get
fills
.Fa out
with the current shape of the shared trace behind the handle
.Fa t ,
for monitoring a long-running dataflow.
Set
.Fa out->size
to
.Li sizeof(dtfl_trace_stats)
first; fields past that size are left alone, so a program built
against an older, shorter structure keeps working.
.Pp
The fields are:
.Bl -tag -width updates
.It Fa layers
the spine's levels, vacant ones included.
.It Fa batches
the batches a cursor over the whole trace would visit, empty batches
included: each in-progress merge counts its two inputs.
.It Fa pending
batches not yet past the physical compaction frontier, which wait
outside the spine
.Pq Xr dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction 3 .
.It Fa merges
levels with a merge in progress.
.It Fa updates
the (key, value, time, difference) updates across all batches.
.It Fa bytes
the bytes the batches' key, value, offset, time and difference columns
occupy, not counting allocation slack.
.El
.Pp
A trace whose readers never advance their compaction holds keeps every
batch:
.Fa batches
and
.Fa pending
grow with each sealed epoch.
A healthy trace keeps
.Fa batches
near the logarithm of
.Fa updates .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns
.Dv DTFL_OK ,
or
.Dv DTFL_EINVAL
if an argument is
.Dv NULL
or
.Fa out->size
is smaller than a field or larger than the structure this library
knows.
Once every reader has dropped the trace, all counts are zero.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A handle kept only for monitoring should give up its compaction holds,
or it will itself keep every batch alive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_trace *watch = dtfl_arranged_trace(a);
dtfl_trace_stats st = { .size = sizeof st };

dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction(watch, NULL, 0);
dtfl_trace_set_physical_compaction(watch, NULL, 0);
/* ... later, on the same worker ... */
if (dtfl_trace_stats_get(watch, &st) == DTFL_OK)
	printf("%zu batches, %zu updates\en", st.batches, st.updates);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_arranged_trace 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_trace_set_logical_compaction 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7
.Sh HISTORY
A libdtfl addition; differential dataflow reports the same information
as logging events
.Pq Pa logging.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
The trace handle belongs to the worker thread that created it.
